# `test/` was renamed to `render/` on 2026-08-22. It was never test code: the production
# renderer imports its map controller from there, and it also holds the render metadata,
# source cache and generated tiles. Sitting beside `tests/` and `test2/`, the name was
# the most misleading thing an outside developer met.
#
# /test/ served a real (noindex) page, so the old paths keep working. 301 rather than
# 302: the move is permanent and there is no reason to make every visitor re-ask.
#
# Since data design phase 3 (PHASE3.md, site-restructure renames.csv) they go straight to the
# map app, not through /render/ (the legacy test app) and then on: one hop, no chain. The
# metadata paths under /test/ still reach the files and Functions now under /render/metadata/.
# The hash (#layers=...) is kept by the browser across a redirect; Pages keeps the query.
#
# /test/sw.js is the exception, and must stay above /test/*: browsers that opened /test/ before
# the rename still hold a worker registered from that address, and a browser refuses a redirect
# when it checks a worker for an update, so a 301 there would leave the old worker (and up to
# 270 MB of its caches) installed for good. It answers 200 with the retired-app kill switch
# (render/sw.js), which unregisters it and clears its caches. Keep it as long as /render/sw.js.
/test/sw.js  /render/sw.js  200
/test/metadata/*  /render/metadata/:splat  301
/test/*  /maps/  301
/test    /maps/  301

# The legacy test apps are retired (site restructure F5, 7 Nov 2026): /render/ was the MapLibre
# rewrite's development harness and /test2/ the app's address before it became the root and then
# /maps/. Their pages answer 301 to the map app, which reads the same hash (layers, lng, lat, and
# z as well as zoom). The workers they registered are retired by the kill switch still served at
# /render/sw.js and /test2/sw.js (those two files, byte for byte the same), so neither address may
# gain a splat rule here. /render/metadata/* keeps answering: the map app and third parties read it.
/render            /maps/  301
/render/           /maps/  301
/render/index.html /maps/  301
/render/build/*    /maps/  301
/test2             /maps/  301
/test2/            /maps/  301
/test2/index.html  /maps/  301

# /maps/test/ was where the MapLibre app was reviewed before it became /maps/. Shared links land
# on the app itself; the page is no longer written.
/maps/test         /maps/  301
/maps/test/  /maps/  301
/maps/test/index.html  /maps/  301

# The Status page sits beside About, at /pages/status.html; /status is its short address.
/status   /pages/status  301
/status/  /pages/status  301

# The Leaflet 1.9.4 files of the retired Leaflet map (archived in fb5d246cad, August 2026) left the
# tree on 7 Nov 2026: no page has loaded them since the MapLibre map took over. Their addresses answer
# with the same release on unpkg, the same bytes (the stylesheet bar its line endings), so a page or
# cache that still asks for them gets what it asked for.
/assets/js/leaflet-1.9.4.js  https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js  301
/assets/css/leaflet-1.9.4.css  https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css  301
/assets/css/images/*  https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/images/:splat  301

